    mainDescription:
      "<p>The timeline reminder suite configures automated reminder cadences and shared dashboard reporting for the specific forty five day identification and one hundred eighty day completion deadlines governing a Phoenix, AZ investor's Section 1031 exchange. Unlike a general purpose calendar reminder, this suite is built specifically around exchange mechanics, meaning reminders account for the exact regulatory deadline dates, interim milestones such as inspection periods and lender commitment dates, and the reality that these federal deadlines cannot be extended even when a delay is caused by circumstances outside anyone's control, making proactive awareness more valuable than after the fact problem solving.</p><h3>Configuring Reminders Around Exchange Mechanics</h3><p>Custom reminder templates reference Phoenix's Mountain Standard Time zone and the investor's actual deadline dates, rather than generic countdown messaging, so every notification clearly states what action is due and by when, reducing the ambiguity that can arise when an investor receives reminders from multiple sources with slightly different framing. A shared dashboard presents every task with filterable views, so an investor, their qualified intermediary, and their advisors can each look at the same underlying data organized around their own priorities, whether that means viewing tasks by deadline, by responsible party, or by completion status. Completion history is retained within the dashboard, providing a running record of what has already been accomplished, which is useful both for the investor's own peace of mind and as documentation if a question about the exchange timeline arises later during tax preparation or in a conversation with an attorney.</p><h3>Escalation and Secure Document Access</h3><p>Escalation configuration allows overdue items to trigger increased outreach automatically, ensuring that a missed reminder does not simply go unnoticed until the next scheduled check in, and instead prompts a follow up before the underlying deadline arrives. Secure links are included directly within reminder notifications, so stakeholders can access relevant documents and act on outstanding items immediately rather than needing to search through email threads or separate file storage systems to find what a reminder is actually referring to. A reminder calendar documents the message content planned for each milestone throughout the exchange, giving investors visibility into what communications are coming before they arrive rather than being surprised by an unfamiliar notification during a busy stretch of the transaction. Dashboard access instructions are provided to both investors and their advisors, and a notification archive maintains a record of all outreach and responses throughout the exchange, which becomes a useful reference if the timeline needs to be reconstructed for any reason after closing, including supporting the documentation an accountant may want when preparing Form 8824 for the completed transaction.</p><p>Setup begins with a short onboarding conversation confirming exactly which milestones matter for the specific exchange, since a straightforward forward exchange requires a simpler reminder set than a reverse exchange or an improvement exchange, each of which carries additional milestones tied to the exchange accommodation titleholder relationship or construction draw schedule respectively. We configure separate reminder tracks for the investor and for each advisor added to the suite, so a lender receives financing specific reminders while an attorney receives document review reminders, rather than every party receiving an identical, undifferentiated stream of notifications that can lead to important items being overlooked amid less relevant ones. The dashboard also supports a simple end of exchange summary view once closing is complete, consolidating the full milestone history into a single record that investors have found useful when working with their CPA during tax season, since it eliminates the need to reconstruct dates and completed tasks from memory or scattered email searches months after the transaction has closed.</p><p>Investors coordinating a multi property exchange under the two hundred percent or ninety five percent rule receive a consolidated view spanning every identified property rather than a separate reminder stream for each one, since tracking several parallel closing timelines through disconnected notifications tends to increase, rather than reduce, the chance that a milestone on a lower priority property is overlooked. The suite integrates directly with the identification notice itself, so once a property is added to or removed from the identification list, the associated reminder set updates automatically rather than requiring a manual reconfiguration that could introduce a gap in coverage during a busy period of the exchange.</p>",
